cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "LeafPro: la hoja, carácter por carácter — a browser-based app for teaching leaf morphology"
abstract: >-
  LeafPro is a self-contained web application for teaching leaf morphology, entirely in the
  browser, with no installation and no server. A parametric leaf engine draws every figure in
  the app from a small model (blade shape × apex × base × margin × pinnate or palmate lobing ×
  venation), including compound leaves and leaf surfaces. It covers the parts of the dicot and
  grass leaf, simple versus compound leaves with the axillary-bud test, phyllotaxy with a
  golden-angle simulator, an atlas of more than 140 illustrated terms, an interactive cross-section of the blade from the upper to the lower face (haz and envés), modified leaves (tendrils, spines, bracts, spathes, cataphylls, pitchers and snap traps), leaf duration with definitions and
  example species with an emphasis on Mexico, a leaf builder that writes the botanical
  description as characters are combined, generative self-assessment, and a classroom mode
  for projecting question-first plates and printing study or exam sheets. The interface is in
  Spanish and English, with a light and a dark theme.
type: software
